## Reproducing a run

```bash
git clone <this-repo> && cd <this-repo>
madbench init
madbench run tests/<name>.yml --dry-run
madbench run tests/<name>.yml
```

## Workspace layout

```text
tests/      # pipeline definitions
scripts/    # executable scripts used by pipeline steps
inputs/     # repository resources staged for steps
results/    # live report.json, CSV views, and published artifacts
scratch/    # work directories and disposable step caches
logs/       # orchestration plus per-execution stdout and stderr
gridpacks/  # reusable, repository-managed gridpack inputs
MadGraph/   # local MadGraph installations
analysis/   # notebooks and post-processing
```

Each pipeline declares a global `matrix`, optional `zip` relationships,
top-level resources to stage under `inputs`, and an ordered `steps` list.
Scripts receive positional values from `with`. Specific staged files should
be passed with:

```yaml
with:
  proc_card:
    input: ${{ matrix.proc_card }}
```

The YAML path remains workspace-relative; MadBench passes an absolute path
below `$MADBENCH_INPUTS` to the step.

Step artifacts use the same absolute-path handoff:

```yaml
artifacts:
  workspace:
    path: workspace

# In a later step:
with:
  workspace: ${{ steps.prepare.artifacts.workspace }}
```

The artifact `path` is relative to its producer's workdir. Omitting `publish`
keeps it available to downstream steps and caches without copying it into
permanent results. Adding a safe relative `publish` path copies it to
`results/.../artifacts/<step>/<mg_version>/<rep>/<publish>`.

To keep a test's execution work and cache outside the workspace, set its work
root:

```yaml
workdir: /scratch/madbench
```

This creates `/scratch/madbench/<test>_<timestamp>/` for staged inputs and
step workdirs, and `/scratch/madbench/.madbench-cache/` for default step
caches. Durable results still go to the workspace `results_dir`.

Every run creates:

```text
results/<pipeline>/<hostname>_<timestamp>/
├── test.yml
├── report.json       # atomically updated deep execution record
├── results.csv       # live final-step repetition rows
├── step_timings.csv  # live row for every step execution
├── summary.csv       # live aggregate statistics and completion counts
├── attempts/
│   └── try_0/        # attempt-scoped report/results/timings
└── artifacts/        # <step>/<mg_version>/<rep>/<published path>

logs/<pipeline>/<hostname>_<timestamp>/
├── main.log           # live orchestration narrative
└── <step>/<execution-id>/<repetition>/
    ├── stdout.log
    └── stderr.log
```

The top-level views are created before execution and atomically refreshed
after every recorded step, so they are safe to inspect during multi-day runs.
Final-step repetitions are scheduled outermost: every matrix point completes
rep 1 before rep 2 begins. See the MadBench project README for the complete
pipeline, input-resolution, artifact, output, cache, and repetition reference.

